meminfo - displays user and kernel heap memory usage

Description:
The 'meminfo' command retrieves and prints information about two separate heaps:

1. User program heap - the malloc heap of the currently running user program.
   This shows heap start and end addresses, maximum heap size, bytes actually
   used, bytes currently free in the allocator, and memory still available for
   expansion before reaching the heap limit.

2. Kernel heap - the kernel kmalloc heap, retrieved via a system call.
   This shows the same metrics for kernel-side dynamic memory.

Values are displayed in a human-readable format using appropriate units (B, KB, MB, GB).

Usage:
meminfo

Examples:
meminfo
